  "notes": "{皮|かわ} is a versatile word referring to outer coverings: animal/human skin, fruit peels, and leather.\n\nCOMMON VERBS:\n- {皮|かわ}を{剥|む}く: to peel (fruit/vegetables)\n- {皮|かわ}が{剥|む}ける: skin peels off\n- {皮|かわ}を{脱|ぬ}ぐ: to shed skin (snakes)\n\nCOMPARE SIMILAR WORDS:\n- {皮|かわ}: skin, peel, leather (general outer covering)\n- {革|かわ}: leather (processed animal hide)\n- {肌|はだ}: skin (human, focusing on texture/complexion)\n- {皮膚|ひふ}: skin (medical/formal term)\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {毛皮|けがわ}: fur\n- {皮肉|ひにく}: irony, sarcasm\n- {鳥|とり}の{皮|かわ}: chicken skin",
